@startuml
' Weighted alias evidence is request-scoped and only active during lexical grounding.
title Weighted Alias Evidence — Scoped Lexical Grounding

start
:Frozen semantic contract;
if (Lexical grounding active?) then (yes)
  :Use only aliases actually matched
by the current grounding path;
  if (Model already known with certainty?) then (yes)
    :Model evidence = KnownWithCertainty\n(distinct provenance, not a 1-100 weight);
  else (no)
    :Model evidence = Unknown\nNo model-level weight is invented;
  endif

  fork
    :Entity alias match;
    :Evaluate entity weight only;
  fork again
    :Field alias match;
    :Evaluate field weight only;
  fork again
    :Relationship alias match;
    :Evaluate relationship weight only;
  end fork

  :Never average field/relationship
weights into entity/table weight;
  if (Every grounded scope >= minimum?) then (yes)
    :Evidence is conclusive;
  else (no)
    :Evidence is inconclusive;
    :Do not narrow solely from weight;
  endif
else (no)
  :Weight feature is inert;
  :No lexical evidence to gate;
endif

:Authorization remains a separate boundary;
:Alias weight never grants capability;
stop
@enduml
